  "explanation": "The whole question is the short branch in the middle: the writer asks the shell where home is, and the tool reads from somewhere Windows decides, and nothing today notices when those are not the same file. Compare [the three ways out](#the-options) against the box on the left — this script already refuses and explains in four other situations rather than half-succeeding, which is the argument for one of them. Leaves out what the setting itself does, and leaves out the wrappers, which are written inside the clone and never have this problem.",
